\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{Testing energy control of graph slope.} Consider the gravitational and capillary surface terms for a one-dimensional graph,
\[
 E_s(\eta)=\frac g2\int\eta^2dx+\tau\int(\sqrt{1+|\eta'|^2}-1)dx,
 \quad g,\tau>0.
\]
Choose a nonconstant smooth compactly supported $f$, set $\eta_\epsilon(x)=\epsilon^{1/2}f(x/\epsilon)$, and take zero surface potential. Then $\|\eta_\epsilon'\|_\infty=\epsilon^{-1/2}\|f'\|_\infty\to\infty$, whereas
\[
 \int\eta_\epsilon^2=\epsilon^2\int f^2,\qquad
 \int(\sqrt{1+|\eta_\epsilon'|^2}-1)
 \leq\int|\eta_\epsilon'|=\epsilon^{1/2}\int|f'|\to0.
\]
The inequality uses $\sqrt{1+s^2}-1\leq|s|$. Hence these conserved-energy terms cannot by themselves control a Lipschitz continuation criterion.

\paragraph{Why this is only an obstruction to a proof.} The sequence consists of smooth graphs and does not construct a singular water-wave solution. It also does not preserve the report's fixed nonzero impulse constraint, so it cannot refute existence or uniqueness of its minimizers. Its point is narrower: an argument ``energy is conserved, therefore all higher geometric norms remain bounded'' is invalid without an additional estimate. Replacing the exact capillary energy by its quadratic small-slope approximation would hide this issue precisely where slopes become large.

\paragraph{Both missing hypotheses remain.} Global evolution in the actual variational energy space requires a continuation mechanism beyond this surface-energy bound. Uniqueness up to translation of the constrained solitary-wave minimizer is a separate variational question; energy boundedness yields no strict convexity after the nonlinear constraint. Neither source hypothesis, and thus no unconditional orbital-stability conclusion, is proved here.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked scaling and capillary inequality, zero-potential choice, and failure to preserve nonzero impulse; no dynamical blowup is asserted. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked scaling and capillary inequality, zero-potential choice, and failure to preserve nonzero impulse; no dynamical blowup is asserted. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; Additional geometric continuation control and a separate constrained-minimizer uniqueness proof are missing.

Coordinator checked the height, slope, gravity-energy and capillary-energy scaling of the localized graph family. It is not claimed to solve the water-wave evolution or a fixed-impulse constraint. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

